      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I agree merging this is the right thing to do.\n\nMy concern with `[-1]` is not only that we arbitrarily (and non-intuitively, IMO) pick one of the `srcs` as _the_ DTS but also that we do so in a way that is different from how other modules do it as `rust_*` modules use `srcs[0]` as their top-level `.rs` but using `[0]` in this case would make the \"`default` cascade\" harder to use (as `.dtsi` come from the `default` and `.dts` from the module using them).\n\nI initially tried to find a Bash one-liner to filter `$(in)` to only keep the `*.dts` (no matter its index) but that turns out to be more complicated than I thought (if we want to properly handle paths with spaces). I wish I knew Go so that I could write a Soong module for DTs, making the blueprints clearer and the target more robust ... Oh well, I\u0027ll add this to my list!",
